---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="What CS Worlds is, how it works, and how it is licensed.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="About" title="About CS Worlds “Unplugged”" lead="Computer science through unplugged games, for grades 6–12." />
  <section class="on-paper band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article class="card prose" style="margin:0 auto">
        <h2>What it is</h2>
        <p>CS Worlds is a free collection of unplugged games about computer science, computational
          thinking, data science, AI literacy, cybersecurity, and ethics. Each game is set in a world
          with its own story and rules, and is played with paper and cards. This website is where you
          find the games, learn to play them, print what you need, and explore the ideas behind them.</p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>There are no accounts, cookies, or analytics, and the site loads nothing from other
          services. Nobody, student or teacher, gives any personal information to use it.</p>

        <h2 id="license">License</h2>
        <p>Unless otherwise noted, the content is licensed under the
          <a href={SITE.license.url} rel="license">Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
          International License</a>. You may copy, adapt, and share it for noncommercial purposes if you
          give credit and share your adaptations under the same license.</p>

        <h2>Who makes it</h2>
        <p>CS Worlds is designed by {SITE.author}, a computer science educator and designer. The
          project is developed in the open on <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
